  "slug": "resource-updated-2171",
  "summary": "Four recent tools package RNA-seq and single-cell analysis as containerized pipelines or web platforms for direct use.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is workflow infrastructure for transcriptomic analysis rather than new biological resources. RNA-SeqEZPZ provides a containerized Nextflow pipeline with a point-and-click interface spanning FASTQ processing through differential expression and pathway analysis. SCSEQ offers a web platform for single-cell RNA-seq preprocessing, clustering, cell type identification, and trajectory inference. GEfetch2R, an R package with a Docker image, retrieves scRNA-seq and bulk RNA-seq data from public repositories, loads them into R, and benchmarks the subsequent format conversion tools. CRESCENT is a Snakemake workflow covering expression, splicing, transcript usage, and TEs and non-coding elements. The new element is the breadth of end-to-end coverage delivered through accessible interfaces, with CRESCENT alone extending to non-coding features.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-22"
}
